  "question": {
    "text": "Two integers $r$ and $s$ are drawn one at a time without replacement from the set $\\{1,2, \\ldots ., n\\}$. Then $P(r \\leq k / s \\leq k)=$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}}{\\mathrm{n}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}}{\\mathrm{n}-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}-1}{\\mathrm{n}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}-1}{\\mathrm{n}-1}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\n$\\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{r} \\leq \\mathrm{k} / \\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})=\\frac{\\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{r} \\leq \\mathrm{k} \\cap \\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})}{\\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})}$\nNow, $\\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}}{\\mathrm{n}}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{r} \\leq \\mathrm{k} \\cap \\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})=\\frac{{ }^{\\mathrm{k}} C_2}{{ }^{\\mathrm{n}} C_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}(\\mathrm{k}-1)}{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}-1)} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{p}(\\mathrm{r} \\leq \\mathrm{k} / \\mathrm{s} \\leq \\mathrm{k})=\\frac{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}(\\mathrm{k}-1)}{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}-1)}}{\\frac{k}{n}}=\\frac{k-1}{n-1}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}